# shapez2 Factory Planner — Root

Standing directive. On conflict: [`AGENTS.md`](mdc:AGENTS.md) + [`.cursor/rules/workflow.mdc`](mdc:.cursor/rules/workflow.mdc) + more specific glob rules.

## Operating workflow

```text
Problem → Contract brief → PR plan (one purpose) → Approval → Failing tests → Minimal implementation → Gate → Review
```

- ⬜ Restate or confirm **contract brief** before production edits ([`contract-brief.md`](mdc:documents/ai/templates/contract-brief.md))
- ⬜ **One PR · one purpose** — split when scope grows ([`pr-plan.md`](mdc:documents/ai/templates/pr-plan.md))
- ⬜ **Test before production** for contract/regression changes
- ⬜ Agent scoped by **Position · Authority · Acceptance · Stop conditions** ([`AGENTS.md`](mdc:AGENTS.md))
- ⬜ No commit / push / PR / merge unless user explicitly asks
- ⬜ Close with caveman six sections + validation evidence ([`shapez2-core.mdc`](mdc:.cursor/rules/shapez2-core.mdc))

## Self-check (4 steps)

- ⬜ **Stage:** Which workflow stage? (audit · tests-only · implement · docs)
- ⬜ **Boundary:** Which layer/path owns this change?
- ⬜ **Contract:** What invariant must not break? CANON spec linked?
- ⬜ **Verification:** Which pytest/ruff/mypy/black commands will run?

## DO

- ✅ Python 3.12, src layout, line length 100
- ✅ Contract-first TDD for behavior changes
- ✅ Secrets via `.env` / config only
- ✅ Report commands not run + remaining risk
